From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:21:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] clutter: blur with a dual Kawase pyramid in targets pooled by
 size class

The texture is halved a few times and brought back up to half its size,
so every pixel weighs in once and moving content no longer shimmers, and
strips like a taskbar are no longer blurred at full size with long
kernels. Targets are kept by levels and by size rounded up to 64 pixels,
with the framebuffer copy going straight into the first level, so
resizing reuses them instead of allocating new ones every frame.

Upstream-Status: luft-only Kestrel keeps blur targets across frames and the blur radius matching its own glass
